  "summary": "A movement channeling dreams and the unconscious, juxtaposing irrational imagery with meticulous realism.",
  "description": "Founded by André Breton, Surrealism drew on Freudian psychoanalysis to liberate imagination from reason. Visual artists like Dalí, Magritte, Ernst and Tanning rendered impossible scenes — melting clocks, floating rocks, hybrid creatures — with photographic precision or automatic techniques. Its imagery permeated film, fashion, advertising and later internet dream aesthetics. The movement's faith in the unconscious makes it a recurring reference for any aesthetics of the strange.",
